# Security response headers — kemek-qr
#
# Cloudflare Pages applies this file at deploy time. Each path glob
# attaches the indented headers below it to matching responses.
#
# Decisions (Pass 2 security review, 2026-05-15):
# - CSP carries 'unsafe-inline' on script-src and style-src. The
#   load-bearing FOUC firewall script in app.html validates its
#   localStorage input against a literal allowlist before setting
#   data-theme; there are no other inline scripts and no path that
#   renders user-supplied strings into HTML, so the practical XSS
#   surface is ~0 even with 'unsafe-inline'. Svelte's inline
#   `style:--token={value}` syntax also requires 'unsafe-inline' on
#   style-src — no escape from that without giving up the Svelte 5
#   reactive-token pattern. Pinning a SHA-256 of the FOUC script was
#   considered and rejected (any edit invalidates).
# - connect-src 'self' explicitly excludes cloudflareinsights.com.
#   The brand stance ("no third-party assets, no tracking pixels") is
#   load-bearing; if CFWA ever gets accidentally toggled on in the
#   dashboard, CSP enforcement catches it.
# - img-src adds data: + blob: for qr-code-styling's data-URL outputs
#   and the logo preview pipeline.
# - frame-ancestors 'none' + X-Frame-Options: DENY are belt-and-
#   suspenders against clickjacking on every modern + legacy browser.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=(), magnetometer=(), gyroscope=(), accelerometer=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
